{
  "has_bug": true,
  "defect_description": "In source/collator.py, PackedBatchCollator concatenates DOCUMENTS_PER_PACK independent chat documents into a single training sequence and correctly resets position_ids to 0 at each document boundary, but it also sets attention_mask to a dense all-ones tensor covering the whole pack. In the installed transformers version (5.12.1), the automatic 'packed sequence' block-diagonal causal masking (transformers.masking_utils.find_packed_sequence_indices, invoked from _preprocess_mask_arguments/create_causal_mask) is only triggered when the model receives attention_mask=None together with reset position_ids; passing any non-None 2D attention_mask (including all-ones) short-circuits that detection and the model falls back to one plain causal mask spanning the entire packed sequence. As a result, during training, tokens in later documents of a pack can attend to unrelated earlier documents in the same pack (and vice versa for their shared loss computation), contaminating gradients with unrelated conversation context. This was verified two ways: (1) direct inspection of transformers' masking_utils source confirms packed_sequence_mask is None precisely when attention_mask is passed as ones, but is a correct block-diagonal mask when attention_mask=None; (2) using the actual project code (collator.py + model.py) on real training data, perturbing tokens in document 0 of a pack changed document 3's logits by up to 5.6 (max abs diff) with the original attention_mask=ones behavior, versus exactly 0.0 change once attention_mask is omitted -- proving the leak and its fix. This silently changes the intended training behavior (each packed document should be trained as if independent, matching how evaluate.py always scores documents independently) without crashing or producing obviously anomalous loss curves.",
  "repair": {
    "description": "Removed the erroneous attention_mask=torch.ones_like(input_ids) entry from the batch dict returned by PackedBatchCollator in source/collator.py. training.py already filters inputs with `if name in batch`, so omitting the key means attention_mask is no longer passed to the model; the model then receives only input_ids and position_ids, letting transformers auto-detect document boundaries from the position_ids resets and build a correct block-diagonal causal mask so each packed document only attends to itself. Verified end to end (CPU) that the fixed collator still produces finite loss/gradients of the same scale as the original training trace, and that cross-document logit leakage is eliminated (0.0 diff vs 5.6 before the fix).",
    "modified_paths": ["source/collator.py"]
  }
}
